From 7cc69741c081a58ac026c2b290bd7bd366b97acf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Quintin Smits <qd.smits@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 21:31:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(ui): Holders page imports and exports holder files
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Import… and Export… on the Holders page are enabled. Export writes the
document's user holders to a camcraft-components/1 file. Import adds the
holders of such a file as user holders in one undo step (ImportHolders);
a held id takes a new user:holder:<name> id, as Copy as user holder
does. A file that is not correct, or a row that is not a holder, is
refused by name and the document does not change. The MCP tools
export_holders and import_holders use the same command.

Fixes #4389

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
